# KNOWN GAP — LLVM backend never emits the SDL runtime blob; the link fails.
#
# Calling any `xtd.sdl` function builds on the C backend and fails to LINK under
# `--backend=llvm`:
#
#     gg build                 -> rc 0
#     gg build --backend=llvm  -> undefined reference to `gorget_sdl_init'
#                                 undefined reference to `gorget_sdl_quit'
#
# Measured at HEAD (2026-08-17) on this exact six-line program.
#
# ⚠ DISTINCT FROM gorget-arena snag #1, and this fixture is shaped to prove it.
# Snag #1 is a missing C TYPEDEF for a struct defined in an FFI-only module, and
# it fails at shim COMPILE time with `unknown type name 'GorgetSDLWindow'`.
# THIS program mentions no struct at all -- `sdl_init(int)` and `sdl_quit()` are
# both scalar-only -- so the shim compiles fine and the failure lands at LINK:
# the SDL runtime blob was never emitted, so the symbols do not exist. Snag #1's
# stated fix (extend the shim's type-collection walk) emits no function bodies
# and therefore cannot close this. Do not merge the two entries.
#
# In the wild this is what makes `examples/sdl_hello.gg` fail on the LLVM lane
# while building clean on C -- 15 undefined `gorget_sdl_*` references. The two
# sibling examples that fail under LLVM (`gfx_demo`, `breakout`) fail the OTHER
# way, at shim compile, and those two ARE snag #1.
#
# INTENDED: this builds and prints `ok` on BOTH backends. The C backend already
# does; the LLVM backend must emit the same runtime blob when an `xtd.sdl`
# symbol is reachable.
#
# ⚠ This fixture requires the SDL headers/libs that the C lane already needs; it
# is a BUILD-only assertion and is never run (initialising a real video
# subsystem in a test harness would be environment-dependent).
#
# Wired test: known_gap_llvm_sdl_runtime_blob (tests/integration.rs, #[ignore]d).
# It asserts the LLVM build SUCCEEDS, so it fails today and goes green when the
# blob is emitted. Graduate it out of `known_gaps/` that round.
from xtd.sdl import sdl_init, sdl_quit, SDL_INIT_VIDEO

void main():
    sdl_init(SDL_INIT_VIDEO)
    sdl_quit()
    print("ok")
